<article class="env-theorem" id="03UZ">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03UZ">Theorem <span data-tag="03UZ">64.20.1</span> <span class="named">(Finite Coefficients)</span>.</a>  Let $X$ be a scheme of finite type over a finite field $k$. Let $\Lambda $ be a finite ring of order prime to the characteristic of $k$ and $\mathcal{F}$ a constructible flat $\Lambda $-module on $X_{\acute{e}tale}$. Then </p>
  <div class="equation">
  \[  L(X, \mathcal{F}) = \det (1 - \pi _ X^*\  T |_{R\Gamma _ c(X_{\bar k}, \mathcal{F})})^{-1} \in \Lambda [[T]].  \]
</div>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Omitted. 
